00:18:47,368 --> 00:18:53,368
In 1818, high-spirited young Fanny Brawne finds herself increasingly intrigued by the handsome
but aloof poet John Keats, who lives next door to her family friends the Dilkes.

4
00:25:03,157 --> 00:25:09,157
After reading a book of his poetry, she finds herself
even more drawn to the taciturn Keats.

5
00:31:18,947 --> 00:31:24,947
Although he agrees to teach her about poetry, Keats cannot act on his reciprocated feelings
for Fanny, since as a struggling poet he has no money to support a wife.

