12
01:15:09,473 --> 01:15:15,473
Bright Star is a 2009 biographical romantic drama film,
written and directed by Jane Campion.

13
01:21:25,263 --> 01:21:31,263
It is based on the last three years of the life of poet John Keats (played by Ben
Whishaw) and his romantic relationship with Fanny Brawne (Abbie Cornish).

14
01:27:41,052 --> 01:27:47,052
Campion's screenplay was inspired by a 1997 biography of Keats by
Andrew Motion, who served as a script consultant.

15
01:33:56,842 --> 01:34:02,842
Bright Star was in the main competition at the 2009 Cannes Film
Festival, and was first shown to the public on 15 May 2009.

16
01:40:12,631 --> 01:40:18,631
The film's title is a reference to a sonnet by Keats titled "Bright star, would I
were stedfast as thou art", which he wrote while he was with Brawne.

